--- a/src/hal/components/lincurve.comp
+++ b/src/hal/components/lincurve.comp
@@ -11,6 +11,12 @@
 The (x,y) points are defined by the x-val-NN and y-val-NN parameters which need
 to be set in the HAL file using "setp" commands.
 
+The x-val-NN breakpoints must be finite and strictly increasing.  Each
+y-val-NN must remain paired with the x-val-NN at the same index; y values
+need not be monotonic.  The component does not validate breakpoint ordering.
+An incorrectly ordered table can give different outputs for the same input
+depending on previous inputs.  Updating several table parameters while the
+realtime function is running is not an atomic table replacement.
+
 The maximum number if (x,y) points supported is 16.
 
 For input values less than the x-val-00 breakpoint the y-val-00 is returned. 
